@@ -173,3 +173,7 @@ Changes from version 2.8 which are relevant for users:
     (see \issue{658}). Previously each wall acted on half of the periodic domain, so that e.g. an upper and a lower wall at +-2 on a torsion
     pushed it out of the interval [-2,2] when its value was beyond +-(pi-2). AT must now be within the periodic domain of the argument.
     Results are unchanged when the argument stays further than half a period from AT.
+  - PLUMED now stops with an error when two actions try to write the same file (see \issue{802}), e.g. two \ref METAD actions
+    without the FILE keyword, which both used the default HILLS file. Previously the file was silently corrupted: one action was writing
+    on the backup copy (e.g. bck.0.HILLS) and only the last one on HILLS, or, when restarting, the lines of the two actions were interleaved.
+    The same file is detected also when it is referred to with a different path (e.g. ./HILLS). /dev/null can still be shared.
